WEBVTT

00:02.043 --> 00:05.422
You're pretty perceptive.

00:05.505 --> 00:07.716
You must be really observant.

00:08.883 --> 00:11.011
That intense light the other day.

00:11.511 --> 00:14.180
Maybe Mr. Qifrey would know something.

00:15.015 --> 00:17.559
Hey, Mr. Qifrey?

00:18.226 --> 00:21.938
There's something I'd like to ask you.

00:27.402 --> 00:28.528
That's

00:29.279 --> 00:30.822
wonderful!

00:30.905 --> 00:31.740
Huh?

00:31.823 --> 00:34.200
Ask me anything.

00:34.284 --> 00:37.203
If it's about magic, I'm happy to answer.

00:37.287 --> 00:40.206
So then, Tartah,
what is it you want to know?

00:40.290 --> 00:42.208
What?!

00:42.292 --> 00:45.420
It's hard to tell him
that's not the kind of question I meant.

00:45.503 --> 00:47.797
He's practically beaming. Makes it tough.

00:47.881 --> 00:48.840
Excuse me.

00:49.591 --> 00:51.009
Are you the person from earlier?

00:51.634 --> 00:53.178
Please come inside.

00:53.678 --> 00:55.096
Right this way.

00:57.682 --> 01:01.561
It's a cold brought on by exhaustion
and lack of sleep.

01:04.189 --> 01:07.358
It seems she hasn't been sleeping well
for a while.

01:07.942 --> 01:11.112
She should be fine
with proper rest and nutrition.

01:11.613 --> 01:14.574
Just to be safe,
let's have her rest here tonight.

01:15.784 --> 01:17.077
Thank you.

01:17.702 --> 01:18.661
Honestly.

01:19.829 --> 01:24.000
I don't know what kind of harsh training
witches go through,

01:24.084 --> 01:26.002
but she's still just a child.

01:26.086 --> 01:30.423
The adults around her
need to look after her properly.

01:35.178 --> 01:36.513
She's absolutely right.

01:37.430 --> 01:39.265
I'm sorry, Coco.

01:59.828 --> 02:02.413
I hope this helps a little.

02:02.914 --> 02:04.249
If it was hard,

02:04.332 --> 02:06.960
she didn't have to push herself
until she collapsed.

02:07.877 --> 02:09.629
Sometimes, your body, your heart,

02:10.296 --> 02:13.091
even your actions,
stop doing what you want them to.

02:13.716 --> 02:18.054
Until recently, Coco knew nothing
about the world of magic.

02:18.596 --> 02:20.390
Even if she acted cheerful,

02:20.473 --> 02:23.393
she was probably full of anxiety inside.

02:26.771 --> 02:28.356
Knew nothing?

02:28.857 --> 02:31.192
She's the Outsider?

02:31.276 --> 02:32.610
Her?

02:32.694 --> 02:33.778
Tartah.

02:34.445 --> 02:37.323
It seemed like there was something
you wanted to ask me,

02:37.907 --> 02:39.534
but could it wait?

02:40.952 --> 02:42.412
Now may not be the best time.

02:47.375 --> 02:48.835
I understand.

02:49.502 --> 02:51.171
Please don't worry about it.

02:54.007 --> 02:55.884
Then I should get going.

02:55.967 --> 02:58.261
Thanks. Take care.

03:12.400 --> 03:13.526
Back then,

03:14.027 --> 03:17.906
for a split second,
I could've sworn I felt an icy glare.

03:19.574 --> 03:22.035
Maybe I was just imagining it.

03:23.745 --> 03:24.787
No, no.

03:24.871 --> 03:27.874
Only witches are allowed on this ferry.

03:27.957 --> 03:31.002
If you're from that island,
where's your witch hat?

03:31.085 --> 03:32.086
THE SILVER PROMISE

03:32.170 --> 03:34.672
I can't let anyone through
without proof they're a witch.

03:34.756 --> 03:35.924
I have it right here.

03:38.760 --> 03:40.511
What? It's gone!

03:40.595 --> 03:41.596
Yeah?

03:41.679 --> 03:43.181
But I crossed this morning--

03:43.264 --> 03:44.766
Like I care!

03:44.849 --> 03:48.269
We get plenty of little punks
trying to sneak in with that story.

03:49.395 --> 03:50.355
Hey!

03:50.438 --> 03:52.482
Get back here!

03:54.400 --> 03:56.569
I can't get home without my hat.

03:57.070 --> 03:58.238
I've gotta find it.

03:58.988 --> 04:01.491
Her breathing has settled.

04:04.786 --> 04:07.497
If she gets rest like this,
she'll recover just fine.

04:08.331 --> 04:09.457
Thank goodness.

04:10.041 --> 04:11.251
Though, I have to say,

04:11.960 --> 04:15.255
the air in just this area
is cool and refreshing.

04:15.338 --> 04:17.215
Magic really is amazing.

04:17.715 --> 04:19.676
Doctors are amazing too.

04:20.218 --> 04:23.137
Magic can’t cure illnesses,
so this is all I can do.

04:23.221 --> 04:26.557
Still, it should help her recover.

04:26.641 --> 04:29.269
I wish we could use magic too.

04:32.480 --> 04:33.815
Yes.

04:35.483 --> 04:36.901
Doctor, are you here?

04:37.485 --> 04:39.946
There's a fire
over at the tavern up north!

04:41.489 --> 04:43.074
We're trying to help the injured,

04:43.157 --> 04:45.868
but there are too many drunkards,
and we can't...

04:45.952 --> 04:47.412
Whoa...

04:48.246 --> 04:49.831
You a witch?

04:49.914 --> 04:52.667
And a water witch at that? Perfect.

04:53.251 --> 04:55.378
Come with us and help put out the fire.

04:55.461 --> 04:57.922
Witches are supposed to help
citizens in need, right?

04:58.006 --> 05:00.758
Wait, I can't!

05:00.842 --> 05:02.593
I can't leave here right now.

05:02.677 --> 05:03.886
It's okay.

05:04.887 --> 05:06.556
Please go with them.

05:06.639 --> 05:08.308
It's a witch's job, after all.

05:11.561 --> 05:13.563
All right. I'll be back soon.

05:14.355 --> 05:15.982
Get some rest, okay?

05:17.442 --> 05:18.901
Then let's go.

05:18.985 --> 05:20.320
Thank you.

05:20.403 --> 05:21.988
How bad is it?

05:22.071 --> 05:24.324
The fire was still small when I left,

05:24.407 --> 05:26.409
but if we don't hurry, who knows.

05:28.870 --> 05:30.538
I put on a brave face.

05:31.205 --> 05:34.208
The truth is,
I'm a little scared to be alone.

05:40.298 --> 05:43.134
I've looked everywhere,
but it wasn't anywhere.

05:43.217 --> 05:45.053
- This is the only place left--
- Let's go!

05:48.806 --> 05:51.225
Pardon the intrusion.

06:05.406 --> 06:07.033
My hat...

06:08.201 --> 06:09.285
There it is!

06:12.580 --> 06:15.750
Thank goodness. Now I can go home.

06:23.341 --> 06:24.634
She's having a nightmare?

06:26.761 --> 06:29.222
Hey, you okay?

06:31.849 --> 06:33.935
Tartah?

06:35.645 --> 06:38.356
You scared me. Why are...

06:39.899 --> 06:41.401
Are you okay?

06:42.402 --> 06:44.529
You look worse than before.

06:45.279 --> 06:47.782
Is anyone here?

06:48.616 --> 06:52.161
There has got to be a doctor around.
Where's Mr. Qifrey?

06:52.245 --> 06:55.248
They all went north. There was a fire...

06:55.331 --> 06:56.165
What?

06:57.041 --> 06:58.960
That's why people were out earlier.

06:59.460 --> 07:01.421
What do I do? When are they coming back?

07:01.921 --> 07:03.923
Maybe I should go get them.

07:08.511 --> 07:10.138
For now, I need to do something.

07:10.930 --> 07:13.099
You should take a fever reducer.

07:13.599 --> 07:16.978
Remember the Tranquileaf?
The one from before?

07:17.687 --> 07:20.523
It helps with fevers and coughs.

07:21.107 --> 07:23.192
There must be some within reach.

07:33.244 --> 07:35.580
They're not labeled!

07:36.164 --> 07:39.208
No way!
Who keeps medicine without labels?!

07:39.292 --> 07:42.170
What if someone makes a mistake?!
It'd be bad news.

07:43.713 --> 07:46.132
They all seem like
slightly different shades.

07:47.383 --> 07:50.595
Everyone else must be able
to tell them apart by color.

07:54.098 --> 07:55.641
This again.

07:56.476 --> 07:58.644
Everyone assumes
we all see the same world.

07:59.562 --> 08:01.731
Like that's just a given.

08:02.607 --> 08:04.108
With Silverwash Syndrome,

08:04.192 --> 08:07.570
using pigments for complex magic
is going to be impossible.

08:07.653 --> 08:10.615
He'll never be more than second-rate
as a magic supplier.

08:10.698 --> 08:13.242
It's fine while he's a kid, but...

08:13.326 --> 08:15.703
Good thing you're good at carving pens.

08:17.622 --> 08:21.542
Everyone has things they can do
and things they can't.

08:22.168 --> 08:24.504
Just do what you can.

08:25.505 --> 08:27.256
Damn it.

08:27.757 --> 08:31.260
A lot of medicinal herbs
are used in magical dyes.

08:31.344 --> 08:34.472
If I only knew the type. I know exactly
what each one of them does.

08:34.972 --> 08:37.058
I can't do anything when it matters.

08:37.975 --> 08:41.437
In a world where everything looks silver,

08:42.021 --> 08:44.649
I can't even see any possibilities.

08:48.402 --> 08:50.571
Tartah...

08:53.616 --> 08:56.160
Sorry, I'm useless.

08:56.244 --> 08:58.579
You're the one who's suffering.

09:02.959 --> 09:04.460
Right. Water.

09:06.295 --> 09:08.464
You want water, right?

09:09.048 --> 09:10.424
Here you go.

09:14.637 --> 09:15.596
Thank you.

09:19.767 --> 09:21.602
A vapor bubble...

09:21.686 --> 09:23.521
Come to think of it,

09:23.604 --> 09:26.774
this is what Gramps always uses
when he makes conjuring ink.

09:27.275 --> 09:28.359
That's it!

09:28.442 --> 09:30.945
With this, I can separate the liquid
from the medicine.

09:31.696 --> 09:34.365
If I remove the water it's dissolved in,

09:34.949 --> 09:36.909
maybe I can figure out what's mixed in.

09:39.328 --> 09:41.539
Tranquileaf is a powdered medicine.

09:41.622 --> 09:43.457
It's dried and ground.

09:44.041 --> 09:46.210
So if I look for something
in powdered form...

09:47.503 --> 09:49.714
Not the ones that crystallize.

09:50.965 --> 09:53.634
Not the ones that glow
in the moonlight either.

09:55.720 --> 09:58.848
And not the ones that lose liquid.

09:59.932 --> 10:02.476
The smell isn't distinctive,

10:02.560 --> 10:04.770
so I can rule out
the strong-smelling ones.

10:06.939 --> 10:08.232
Then that leaves...

10:14.905 --> 10:16.532
Three more.

10:17.491 --> 10:20.536
Damn it! I got this far.

10:20.620 --> 10:23.748
I made it this far...

10:24.749 --> 10:27.418
And that's as far as I can go.

10:31.255 --> 10:32.882
Sorry, Coco.

10:34.258 --> 10:36.260
I tried my best,

10:36.761 --> 10:38.846
but I guess this is beyond me.

10:41.098 --> 10:43.934
Why did I think I could do something?

10:45.186 --> 10:46.937
I knew better.

10:47.605 --> 10:49.440
I knew I couldn't.

10:53.361 --> 10:55.029
That's not true.

10:56.364 --> 10:59.784
Magic exists to help people do

11:01.410 --> 11:04.205
what they can't do on their own.

11:05.581 --> 11:06.916
Do you have a pen and ink?

11:07.875 --> 11:09.251
I do.

11:09.335 --> 11:11.212
One I'm still carving.

11:32.608 --> 11:33.776
Are you okay?

11:34.652 --> 11:35.736
Yeah.

11:37.655 --> 11:39.740
What spell are you drawing?

11:39.824 --> 11:43.119
Will it make you feel better?

11:43.703 --> 11:47.039
No, not me.

11:47.123 --> 11:48.332
Not just me.

11:49.625 --> 11:51.168
You and I, Tartah.

11:51.669 --> 11:54.296
It's a spell to help both of us.

11:56.048 --> 11:56.882
Huh?

11:57.591 --> 11:58.718
Me too?

12:00.678 --> 12:02.888
A spell to help me too?

12:03.514 --> 12:05.391
What kind of spell is it?

12:06.892 --> 12:08.394
This is an Earth Sigil.

12:09.061 --> 12:12.648
Digging tunnels, breaking rock into sand...

12:12.732 --> 12:15.484
It's a spell that has helped me
countless times.

12:16.318 --> 12:18.404
Why that one?

12:19.196 --> 12:21.532
"When the arrow changes,
the spell changes."

12:22.324 --> 12:25.494
I'm drawing the arrow of destruction
upside down.

12:26.245 --> 12:28.789
Normally,
it's a spell that turns things to dust.

12:30.499 --> 12:32.835
The upside-down arrow...

12:34.462 --> 12:37.548
It becomes a spell that gives form
to loose material.

12:37.631 --> 12:38.674
Yep.

12:40.217 --> 12:42.678
And that's why, if it's you, Tartah,

12:43.345 --> 12:46.599
you know the true form of so many things.

12:47.099 --> 12:49.059
You can work out the answer

12:49.935 --> 12:52.271
from everything you've learned.

12:55.983 --> 12:57.651
- Huh?
- Hmm?

12:58.986 --> 13:01.405
It's no good when I'm worn out.

13:01.489 --> 13:03.199
My lines are shaky and wobbly.

13:03.282 --> 13:04.533
Hey.

13:05.034 --> 13:07.953
I just need to draw the same shape neatly, right?

13:08.037 --> 13:11.540
With better balance, if possible.

13:12.541 --> 13:16.086
Drawing is one thing,
but I'm good at judging balance.

13:17.338 --> 13:19.089
It's basically what I do all the time.

13:30.309 --> 13:33.103
Actually, about this arrow,

13:33.187 --> 13:37.441
can I draw them left and right,
and not just top and bottom?

13:37.942 --> 13:42.238
Something three-dimensional
has to be shaped from every angle.

13:42.321 --> 13:44.406
As it is now, there are gaps.

13:44.490 --> 13:47.368
I think those spots won't form properly.

13:47.451 --> 13:48.536
So maybe...

13:48.619 --> 13:50.204
Oh, sorry!

13:50.287 --> 13:52.122
I changed your spell without asking.

13:52.623 --> 13:54.375
No, that's okay.

13:54.458 --> 13:57.127
It's just a basic spell. Besides,

13:58.087 --> 14:00.506
if your own ideas changed the outcome,

14:00.589 --> 14:04.009
then it's your spell now, Tartah.

14:07.555 --> 14:08.889
Give it a try.

14:09.598 --> 14:11.892
Okay. I'll try it.

15:13.579 --> 15:14.705
I did it.

15:17.374 --> 15:18.626
I did it.

15:18.709 --> 15:20.544
Just for a second, but I did it.

15:20.628 --> 15:22.296
I really did it.

15:22.379 --> 15:23.422
Yes!

15:23.964 --> 15:26.300
Whoa, sorry! You need medicine!

15:26.842 --> 15:28.302
That was close.

15:28.886 --> 15:31.555
None of these were Tranquileaf.

15:31.639 --> 15:34.266
I assumed it had to be here.

15:34.808 --> 15:35.643
Okay.

15:38.145 --> 15:41.440
I'll use this spell
to search the herb room!

15:41.523 --> 15:43.192
With this spell, I can find it.

15:56.455 --> 15:58.582
It's a bit like our house.

16:04.964 --> 16:07.466
Thornbark, Millflower,

16:07.549 --> 16:10.219
Seabriar, Sleeping WIllow,

16:10.302 --> 16:11.720
and Drizzlebee hive...

16:12.930 --> 16:13.973
I know them.

16:14.473 --> 16:18.227
Every shape is exactly like the ones
I learned from books.

16:19.311 --> 16:20.479
Amazing...

16:21.939 --> 16:23.649
Every time I hold up the seal,

16:24.149 --> 16:26.568
it's like the world comes into focus.

16:28.570 --> 16:30.239
Everything I've learned

16:30.823 --> 16:33.117
is showing me the answer.

16:33.993 --> 16:36.203
Being able to do more than I could before...

16:37.329 --> 16:38.455
It feels so...

16:39.707 --> 16:40.958
so...

16:43.377 --> 16:44.461
I found it.

16:47.715 --> 16:49.299
This is the Tranquileaf!

16:49.800 --> 16:51.301
I've gotta get it to her quick.

16:51.385 --> 16:52.386
Hey, you!

16:52.469 --> 16:55.055
What do you think you're doing?

16:57.224 --> 16:59.643
You thought no one was here?

16:59.727 --> 17:01.645
Impossible.

17:01.729 --> 17:05.190
We'd never leave
a hospital completely unattended.

17:05.691 --> 17:07.901
And the medicines don't have labels

17:07.985 --> 17:10.279
to stop people from tampering with them.

17:10.362 --> 17:14.700
You could have given the wrong medicine.

17:14.783 --> 17:16.118
I'm sorry.

17:16.201 --> 17:17.911
I was in a panic.

17:17.995 --> 17:21.498
Wanting to help your friend is admirable.

17:21.999 --> 17:24.418
But medicine can be poison too.

17:25.002 --> 17:27.796
You need the proper knowledge.

17:28.297 --> 17:32.176
Though, in this case,
Tranquileaf was the correct answer.

17:32.760 --> 17:35.012
Are you knowledgeable about herbs?

17:35.095 --> 17:37.056
Do you have an interest in medicine?

17:37.139 --> 17:39.683
Huh? Well, I'm...

17:39.767 --> 17:41.810
Oh? That hat...

17:42.394 --> 17:45.564
So you're a witch's apprentice.

17:51.612 --> 17:53.822
We've finished carrying out the injured.

17:53.906 --> 17:55.866
That's a relief.

17:56.366 --> 17:58.327
Thank you for your help.

17:59.161 --> 18:01.121
The fire is under control now.

18:01.205 --> 18:03.665
Do you think I can leave things here
to you?

18:04.374 --> 18:05.793
I'm worried about my apprentice.

18:05.876 --> 18:08.212
Hey, now, where do you think you're going?

18:08.295 --> 18:11.215
We've still got cleanup to do!

18:11.298 --> 18:16.011
You witches just wave magic around
and have it easy, right?

18:16.095 --> 18:19.139
In times like this, you ought to be
the first ones pitching in!

18:19.223 --> 18:20.724
I'm counting on you, pal.

18:20.808 --> 18:24.686
Well, it's actually not that easy.

18:25.270 --> 18:27.856
An Outsider wouldn't understand.

18:28.857 --> 18:32.319
Please don't worry about it and go.
My apprentice and I will handle things.

18:32.402 --> 18:33.862
Thank you.

18:39.618 --> 18:42.037
It's not easy nor simple.

18:42.121 --> 18:43.539
Not in the slightest.

18:44.498 --> 18:46.542
Otherwise,

18:46.625 --> 18:49.545
no one would be struggling or suffering.

19:11.316 --> 19:12.693
It's easier to breathe.

19:13.694 --> 19:14.695
I'm glad.

19:15.279 --> 19:16.864
I guess the medicine worked.

19:17.364 --> 19:19.074
Thank you, Tartah.

19:20.117 --> 19:20.951
No...

19:21.827 --> 19:25.080
If anyone, I was the one who was helped.

19:30.627 --> 19:32.337
Witches are amazing.

19:35.007 --> 19:37.092
Aren't witches amazing?

19:40.679 --> 19:44.933
You had me worried
when you didn't come home after dark.

19:45.017 --> 19:46.602
Sorry, Gramps.

19:46.685 --> 19:49.897
Thank you for letting me know, Qifrey.

19:49.980 --> 19:52.608
Not at all. You'd do the same.

19:52.691 --> 19:54.610
Oh, right. So I...

19:55.402 --> 19:59.198
wanted to ask you about the light
I saw at the house the other day.

20:00.199 --> 20:01.325
- Light?
- Light?

20:01.825 --> 20:02.659
Huh?

20:03.285 --> 20:04.995
Never mind.

20:05.704 --> 20:08.498
You push yourself too hard too.

20:08.582 --> 20:10.250
You take care of yourself.

20:11.168 --> 20:13.670
Maybe I was mistaken.

20:14.171 --> 20:16.715
I'll look into it myself again,

20:16.798 --> 20:18.592
about that intense light.

20:20.093 --> 20:21.511
The ferry is leaving.

20:23.096 --> 20:24.306
Master.

20:24.389 --> 20:26.516
Sorry to keep you waiting.

20:27.309 --> 20:28.518
The ferry is departing.

20:35.567 --> 20:36.568
Tartah.

20:37.361 --> 20:38.612
See you around.

20:45.869 --> 20:47.871
We should get going too.

20:48.372 --> 20:49.331
Yes.

20:59.549 --> 21:03.095
I'm going to make a pen for you!

21:03.178 --> 21:06.974
Then I'll cross this river
with my own magic

21:07.057 --> 21:10.060
and deliver it myself! I promise!

21:12.145 --> 21:13.730
Okay!

21:18.819 --> 21:20.737
I'll be looking forward to it!

21:24.199 --> 21:27.536
Looks like you two have gotten close.

21:27.619 --> 21:28.495
Yeah.

21:29.454 --> 21:31.248
She's incredible.

21:31.331 --> 21:35.168
I'm sure,
she'll become someone extraordinary.

21:38.213 --> 21:39.631
And you.

21:40.132 --> 21:42.634
You can become extraordinary too.

21:48.515 --> 21:49.891
I see.

21:49.975 --> 21:53.020
So the nightmares have been
keeping you from sleeping all this time.

21:53.103 --> 21:55.314
Dreams are difficult to deal with.

21:55.814 --> 21:58.191
Spells that force sleep
are forbidden magic.

21:58.900 --> 22:01.278
In any case, let's figure something out.

22:01.778 --> 22:04.323
Every innovation is born from a challenge.

22:05.157 --> 22:06.825
Thank you.

22:06.908 --> 22:09.745
But I think I'm going to be okay now.

22:10.746 --> 22:11.913
Are you sure?

22:12.414 --> 22:14.333
Yes, because

22:15.334 --> 22:18.211
I've found a glimmer of hope.

22:20.130 --> 22:23.800
If reversing an arrow
reverses a spell's effect,

22:24.301 --> 22:27.471
then the same should be true
of forbidden magic.

22:30.432 --> 22:33.977
If I reverse the arrows in the seal
from that picture book,

22:34.644 --> 22:38.106
then maybe I can reverse the spell
that turned my mother to stone.

22:40.067 --> 22:42.527
Hey!

22:44.112 --> 22:45.739
We were so worried!

22:46.323 --> 22:48.825
- Are you better now?
- Yeah!

22:49.868 --> 22:52.245
Thank goodness! I'm so glad!

22:58.085 --> 23:01.838
It seems
your gift didn't have the desired effect.

23:03.340 --> 23:06.009
The Witch Hats haven't all grown soft
in times of peace.

23:06.093 --> 23:08.762
Not all are fools, it seems.

23:09.346 --> 23:11.515
We can't afford to sit back and wait.

23:11.598 --> 23:14.518
We'll have to make our next move.

23:15.018 --> 23:18.021
So then you'll be going next?

23:18.647 --> 23:22.609
You? The embodiment of forbidden magic?

23:23.110 --> 23:24.528
That is the plan.

23:25.946 --> 23:30.075
After all, I can't pass up
the apprentices' test,

23:30.826 --> 23:33.787
the moment they leave
their master's protection.

23:33.912 --> 23:35.914
Subtitle translation by: Emily Noguchi

23:37.082 --> 23:40.919
EPISODE 11
THE TRIAL AT SERPENTBACK CAVE
